v 3
d copulaendog: instrument-free Gaussian copula corrections for endogenous regressors
d
d Corrects endogenous regressors in a linear model when no instrument is
d available. The dependence between the regressor and the structural error is
d modelled with a Gaussian copula and the resulting control function is added
d to the regression. Five cross-sectional estimators behind one interface:
d Park & Gupta (2012), the two-stage copula generated regressor approach of
d Yang, Qian & Xie (2025), the between-regressor correlation variant of
d Haschka (2025), the nonlinear-transformation approach of Breitung, Mayer &
d Wied (2024), and the adjusted estimator of Liengaard et al. (2025). Six
d marginal CDF estimators, bootstrap inference, and a validity report that
d walks the identification requirements the literature states.
d
d This is a port. The econometrics and the reference code are the work of
d Rouven E. Haschka, whose R implementation
d   Copula-based endogeneity corrections in R
d   https://github.com/HashtagHaschka/Copula-based-endogeneity-corrections
d   ORCID https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2916-9745
d every estimator here is derived from, and of Ashwin Malshe, whose packaged
d R version
d   endogCopula
d   https://github.com/ashgreat/endogCopula
d shaped how the port is organised and documented. Please cite both, and the
d paper behind the estimator you use, in any work this contributes to.
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260807
d
d Author: Girish Mallapragada
d Support: https://github.com/girishm77/copulaendog_stata_python/issues
d
